; generated-format instantiation 2026-08-08
|term[designator]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss A minted name bound by convention; fails by dangling or colliding.
  :dual-of @description
  |designation designator
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |designation rigid-designator
    :status hidden
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-descriptors
    :anchor descriptor-kinds
    :projection paraphrase
    A minted name, bound to its referent by convention: someone bound the name to the thing, and that binding is the whole connection — the referent's own properties are irrelevant to it.
  |formal
    :notation <latex:bound(d, r) \; by \; community \; C; \; failure \in \{dangle, collide\}>
  |set-rel :kind subset-of :to @descriptor
  |set-rel :kind disjoint-from :to @description
  |rel :kind held-by :to @naming-community :card 1
  |confused
    :with @description
    If the connection is re-computed from the world's current properties at each use, it is a description — even when it looks like a name (a policed wikilink stem IS a designator; an unpoliced one degrades).
  |invariant
    Kind is per-act (descriptor's [[DECISIONS#d12-location-is-description|D12 location-is-description]] theorem): this same string may be part of a description in an enclosing act.
  |failure-if-misused
    Treating an unmaintained string-match as a designator imports silent retargeting nobody priced.
